.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_OK_ERR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_ok_err
.Nd split a stream into two by a predicate
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft void
.Fo dtfl_stream_ok_err
.Fa "dtfl_stream *st"
.Fa "dtfl_pred_fn pred"
.Fa "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Fa "dtfl_stream **ok"
.Fa "dtfl_stream **err"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_ok_err
splits
.Fa st
into two output streams.
For each record,
.Fa pred
is called with the record; when it returns true the record is sent to
.Fa *ok ,
and when it returns false to
.Fa *err ,
each at the record's time.
Both outputs carry the input's record type.
The two streams are stored through
.Fa ok
and
.Fa err .
.Pp
The context in
.Fa ctx
is passed to
.Fa pred .
When
.Fa ctx
carries a destructor, the operator owns the context and releases it
when the operator is dropped.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_ok_err
returns no value; it stores the two output streams, owned by the scope,
through
.Fa ok
and
.Fa err .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static bool is_even(void *ctx, const void *rec, size_t len) {
	return dtfl_get_u64(rec) % 2 == 0;
}

dtfl_stream *even, *odd;
dtfl_stream_ok_err(in, is_even, DTFL_NOCTX, &even, &odd);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_stream_ok_err
does not return an error code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn ok_err
operator.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its streams belong to the worker thread that built
them and must not be shared.
